SUMMARY: Reserved Seat Demonstration Liquitex Acrylics
DESCRIPTION:Instructor: Kristin Brown\nDate: Saturday\, June 27th\n\nTime
 : 2:30pm-3:30pm\nLocation: Santa Rosa Store\n\nFree!\n\nJoin artist Krist
 en Brown for this informative demonstration where she will share the attr
 ibutes of Liquitex acrylic paint. Attendees will be introduced to the acr
 ylic brand that has been on the forefront of innovation for over 60 years
 . Liquitex offers the most diverse range of professional products\, inclu
 ding seven unique ranges of professional acrylic colors\, innovative medi
 ums\, and a revolutionary range of painting tools to meet the needs of ev
 ery artist. This demo will introduce you to some of the endless possibili
 ties of acrylic color and mediums to inspire you to jump into your next p
 ainting.\n\nArtist's Bio:\n\nKristen Brown is a San Francisco-based paint
 er originally from Saskatchewan\, Canada. She has been an arts educator f
 or nearly 20 years and is currently an artist and representative for Liqu
 itex and Winsor & Newton art materials. Her work explores the themes of d
 issociation\, transience\, memory\, and truth. She has exhibited at the d
 e Young Museum\, San Francisco Arts Commission\, Joyce Gordon Gallery\, a
 nd CICA Museum in South Korea\, among others. Kristen has received grants
  from the Canada Council for the Arts and the Elizabeth Greenshields Foun
 dation in Montreal. Kristen’s work has been featured in Fresh Paint Magaz
 ine (now Create Magazine)\, RELISH Magazine\, Art Maze Magazine\, and els
 ewhere. She holds a BFA in Studio Art from the University of Saskatchewan
  and an MFA in Painting from the Academy of Art University in San Francis
 co.\n\nWebsite: www.kristenbrownart.com http://www.kristenbrownart.com/ •
  Instagram: @kristen_brown_art https://www.instagram.com/kristen_brown_ar
