SUMMARY: Reserved Seat Demonstration: Winsor & Newton Professional Waterc
 olors
DESCRIPTION:Presenter: Ryan Martin\nDate: Sunday\, June 28th\nTime: 12:00
 PM-2:00PM\nLocation: The Classroom inside the Santa Rosa Store\nFree!\n\n
 \nJoin acclaimed artist and educator Ryan Martin for an exclusive reserve
 d seat demonstration featuring Winsor & Newton Professional Watercolors—a
  time-honored medium trusted by generations of artists for its brilliance
 \, transparency\, and superior handling.\n\nRyan Martin\, based in the Sa
 n Francisco Bay Area\, is renowned for his surreal\, dream-like compositi
 ons that intertwine personal heritage and contemporary themes. His work\,
  influenced by his Native American (Mexican/Seri Tribe) and Russian roots
 \, often features subjects haloed by floral and fauna motifs\, reflecting
  cultural symbols and personal narratives. Martin's art has been showcase
 d in prominent venues across the United States\, including the deYoung Mu
 seum in San Francisco and various art fairs in Miami and New York.\n\nIn 
 this engaging session\, Ryan will demonstrate the expressive range of Win
 sor & Newton's professional-grade paints—exploring techniques in layering
 \, glazing\, and dynamic color mixing. With a legacy dating back to 1832\
 , Winsor & Newton continues to set the standard in watercolor with a pale
 tte of highly pigmented\, finely milled colors known for their exceptiona
 l clarity and permanence.\n\nWhether you're refining your technique or ex
 ploring the Winsor & Newton palette for the first time\, this reserved se
 ating event is a must for any watercolor enthusiast.\n\nLimited seating—r
 eserve your spot today!
CATEGORIES:Santa-Rosa,Watercolor,Winsor-&-Newton
