SUMMARY: Intro to Gouache Painting\, for beginner to intermediate
DESCRIPTION:Instructor: Anna Simson\nDates: This is a 4-class series\n\nD
 ays/Times: Saturday\, July 11\, 10-12:30 pm\n\nSunday\, July 19\, 11-1:30
  pm\n\nSunday\, July 26\, 11-1:30 pm\n\nSunday\, Aug. 2\, 11-1:30 pm\nLoc
 ation: Santa Rosa Store\nFee: $140 for 4 classes + a materials fee of $15
 . Instructor will provide paper\, brushes and paint.\n\nNo drawing skills
  are needed!\n\nIn this four-part class\, you will learn:\n\n-basic gouac
 he materials\, paper and brushes\n\n-learn the fundamentals of color mixi
 ng\n\n-learn the difference between traditional and acrylic gouache\n\n-e
 xplore “wet-on-wet” painting\n\n-paint from a small still life\n\n- paint
  two paintings of your choice using the color-mixing skills we learn in t
 he first two paintings\n\n-learn about complementary colors\n\n\nSign up 
 with instructor\, and pay by check\, cash\, or Venmo.\n\n\nEmail to reser
 ve a spot: anna_simson66@yahoo.com mailto:anna_simson66@yahoo.com\n\nBio:
  Anna M. Simson holds a BA and MFA in art practice\, and has taught art m
 aterials workshops\, painting and drawing classes at local colleges\, and
  makes art in her garage studio.
