SUMMARY: Drawing Summer Fruit with Colored Pencil
DESCRIPTION:Instructor: Victoria A. Kochergin\n\nDate: July 18\, 2026\n\n
 Time: 10:30-3:30\n\nLocation: Santa Rosa Store\n\nFee: $95\n\nOne of the 
 signatures of summer is the abundance of fruit growing on the trees. Dive
  into something fun this summer and explore the world of drawing summer f
 ruit with colored pencil! The morning portion of class will focus on colo
 red pencil principles and techniques\, color palette creation\, student e
 xercises and demonstrations. The afternoon portion of the class with be d
 edicated to hands-on drawing time with individual one-on-one assistance. 
 All levels welcomed.\n\nMaterials list to be mailed once registration is 
 completed.\n\nTo register\, please contact Victoria at kochergi@sonic.net
  mailto:kochergi@sonic.net or (707) 479-3336.\n\nVictoria A. Kochergin is
  a local botanical artist and instructor who works with colored pencil an
 d acrylics. Her artwork has been exhibited in galleries\, wineries\, bota
 nical gardens\, international shows and on Alcatraz. For more information
  about Victoria\, please visit her website at www.victoriakochergin.com h
 ttp://www.victoriakochergin.com/\n\nImage: “Bartlett Pear” © 2013
CATEGORIES:Santa-Rosa,Botanical,Colored-Pencil
