SUMMARY: CLASS: OIL PORTRAITS FOR ALL LEVELS
DESCRIPTION:Instructor: Maggie Parr\nDates: Thursday afternoons from July
  16-August 6\n\nTime: 2:30 - 5:30 PM\n\nLocation: San Rafael store\n\nFEE
 : $280 includes all materials (all you need is your own table easel)\n\nR
 egister for class (limited to 12 students): https://www.parrcreate.com/pa
 ge/702307 https://www.parrcreate.com/page/702307\n\nOil painting doesn’t 
 have to be intimidating! In just four weeks\, students will paint a portr
 ait in the indirect style\, starting with a grey value study\, building u
 p with layers\, and finishing with powerful details. The final result alw
 ays surprises people: just by following basic rules\, anyone can create a
  beautiful oil portrait that glows. Even abstract painters can benefit fr
 om learning these techniques.\n\nKnowing how oil painting works give us m
 ore confidence to develop our own authentic creative voice. As Maggie say
 s\, “You gotta learn the rules to break the rules.”\n\n\nMaggie Parr star
 ted her career as a show designer at Walt Disney Imagineering\, where she
  designed theme park attractions around the world. She also expanded into
  book illustration\, murals\, portraits\, comics\, and eventually\, writi
 ng books and scripts for television. She also developed her own painting 
 practice. To that end\, she studied with master teachers like Steve Husto
 n\, Jeremy Lipking\, and Joseph Q. Daily. She got an MFA and taught at th
 e college level\, then developed her own teaching methods for private and
  group study. Today\, Maggie maintains a thriving business creating custo
 m art and designs for corporations\, individuals\, and non-profits. She t
 eaches other artists to utilize classical rendering techniques so they ca
 n confidently break the rules in the service of their own work. And she c
 oaches creatives in search of deeper authenticity\, healing\, and self-ac
 tualization.\n\nWebsite: https://maggieparr.com
CATEGORIES:San-Rafael,Oil-Paint
