SUMMARY: Beginning Gel Printing Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Instructor: Magdalena Bogart\nMonday\, August 24th\n1:00pm-4:
 00PM\nLocation: Santa Rosa Store\n$45.00\n\n\nJoin us for an inspiring ge
 l printing workshop with Magdalena Bogart\, where you'll discover the\nma
 gic of this versatile and expressive art form. You will learn techniques 
 for creating stunning\,\nlayered prints using gel plates\, rich textures\
 , and vibrant colors.\nIf you have wanted to try out this fairly new and 
 very popular way to make your own papers\, whether you are an experienced
  artist or simply curious about the process\, this workshop will provide 
 plenty of creative inspiration and expert insights.\n\nDuring the 3-hours
  workshop\, you will learn the fundamentals of mono-printing with a gel p
 late\,\nincluding an in-depth look at the essential supplies needed. Magd
 alena will discuss different\ntypes of plates and brayers\, as well as th
 e wide range of acrylic paints and inks. You will learn the basics of col
 or theory to ensure great results for your projects.\n\nYou will get to t
 ry out many fun techniques on different papers. Magdalena will introduce 
 various papers for gel printing\, including white copy paper\, calligraph
 y paper\, deli paper\, marker paper\, and more each offering unique effec
 ts.\n\nThe workshop will also explore tools for making marks and textures
 \, from found objects to store-bought supplies. Magdalena will demonstrat
 e how to use stencils - both handmade and purchased\, along with unconven
 tional tools like silicone scrapers\, scrapers\, bubble wrap\, buttons\, 
 yarn\, and cardboard to create stunning patterns.\n\nShe will also cover 
 techniques to embellish your prints incorporating acrylic pens\, Inktense
  pencils and other techniques.\nAdditionally\, Magdalena will provide exp
 ert guidance on cleaning\, caring for\, and storing gel plates to ensure 
 their longevity. To wrap up the session\, she will showcase creative ways
  to use your printed papers\, including ideas for collages\, handmade car
 ds\, and art journals\, along with a take-home list of even more ways to 
 incorporate your gel prints into future projects. Whether you are looking
  to refine your skills or try something new\, this workshop promises to b
 e an engaging and educational experience. Come explore the endless possib
 ilities of gel printing.\n\n\nTo register for this workshop\, please cont
 act Magdalena at: 408.781.2589 or by email\nat: mailto:mag.bogart@gmail.c
 om mailto:mag.bogart@gmail.com mailto:mag.bogart@gmail.com mailto:mag.bog
 art@gmail.com mailto:mag.bogart@gmail.com mag.bogart@gmail.com mailto:mag
 .bogart@gmail.com
CATEGORIES:Santa-Rosa,gel-printing
