SUMMARY: Drawing Succulents with Colored Pencil
DESCRIPTION:Instructor: Victoria A. Kochergin\n\nDate: August 15th\, 2026
 \n\nTime: 10:30-3:30\n\nLocation: Santa Rosa Store\n\nFee: $95\n\n\nLooki
 ng for a summer pastime? Learn how to draw succulents with colored pencil
 ! Perhaps one of the more unique shades of green we find in botanicals is
  that which appear in succulents. With their silvery blue-green hues\, su
 cculents offer the artist an opportunity to explore an exciting new palet
 te. Learn how to draw succulents with their beautiful blue-green hues usi
 ng colored pencil! Class will include exercises\, demonstrations and hand
 s-on drawing time. Although class instruction will gear towards beginning
  and intermediate levels\, instruction will be structured in a way that w
 ill address the needs of the attendees. All levels welcomed.\n\nMaterials
  list to be emailed once registration is completed.\n\nTo register\, plea
 se contact Victoria at kochergi@sonic.net mailto:kochergi@sonic.net or (7
 07) 479-3336.\n\nVictoria A. Kochergin is a local botanical artist and in
 structor who works with colored pencil and acrylics. Her artwork has been
  exhibited in galleries\, wineries\, botanical gardens\, international sh
 ows and on Alcatraz. For more information about Victoria\, please visit h
 er website at www.victoriakochergin.com http://www.victoriakochergin.com/
CATEGORIES:Santa-Rosa,Botanical,Colored-Pencil
