SUMMARY: Afternoon of East Asian Calligraphy with Christine Renden Haggar
 ty
DESCRIPTION:Instructor: Christine Renden Haggarty\nDate: Saturday\, Augus
 t 22nd\nTime: 12:00-3:30PM\nFee: $60.00\nLocation: Santa Rosa Store\n\nTh
 e invention of the brush in 300 B.C. revolutionized civilization at the t
 ime. Up until then\, people were carving in stone or bone or writing with
  sticks in the earth. Because these methods were so slow and unwieldy nec
 essity\, the mother of invention\, the brush was created.\n\nPlease join 
 Christine for this afternoon of brushwork. You will experience three diff
 erent types of script – formal\, semi-cursive and cursive and learn to wr
 ite five different characters in those styles. At the end of the class yo
 u can take your favorite character and write it on a shikishi board.\n\nC
 hristine has studied with several different calligraphy masters over 20 y
 ears. She has participated in exhibitions around the world\; most recentl
 y in San Francisco and Healdsburg. She is the Associate Editor of Heart o
 f the Brush\, a collaborative work with Kazuaki Tanahashi\, published in 
 2016. For more information about Christine go to zenbrush.net http://www.
 zenbrush.net/\n\n\nCost for the afternoon is $60 per class with all mater
 ials included. To enroll contact Christine at zenbrush@yahoo.com mailto:z
 enbrush@yahoo.com
CATEGORIES:Santa-Rosa,Calligraphy,Asian,Brush
