SUMMARY: Workshop: Color Theory 101
DESCRIPTION:Instructor: Suzanne Carson\nDates: Two Saturdays\; September 
 5th & 12th.\nTime: 11:00AM-1:00PM\nLocation: Santa Rosa Store\nPrice: $80
  for 2 sessions or $45 per class\n\nEver wonder how to transform your dra
 wings into vibrant\, expressive works of art? In this 2-hour class\, you’
 ll explore the essentials of color theory\, from primary\, secondary\, an
 d tertiary colors to creating harmony through thoughtful combinations.\n\
 nWe’ll look at color as value\, hue\, and saturation\, as well as its sym
 bolism and emotional impact. You’ll also get a glimpse into the color pal
 ettes of classical and Impressionist masters\, and learn the benefits of 
 working with a limited palette.\n\nThis hands-on class includes practical
  color mixing exercises in acrylics\, using just the three primary colors
  to unlock an infinite range of possibilities.\n\nInstructor will provide
  materials.\n\nPlease text or call Instructor to sign up: 707 888 2083
CATEGORIES:Santa-Rosa,Color
